* {{qualifier|rare:}} [[Mohamud]], [[Mohammud]], [[Mohamid]], [[Mohammid]], [[Muhamud]], [[Muhammid]], [[Muhamid]]
* {{qualifier|rare:}} [[Mohemet]], [[Mehammed]], [[Mohemmed]], [[Mehamet]], [[Mohemed]], [[Mahemed]]
* {{qualifier|exceedingly rare:}} [[Mahemmed]], [[Mahemmet]], [[Mahommat]], [[Mehamid]], [[Mehammad]], [[Mohamit]], [[Mohammat]], [[Mohamut]], [[Mohemmet]], [[Muhamut]], [[Muhemmad]]
* {{qualifier|rare, derived from scientific transliterations of Arabic:}} [[Muħammad]]
{{rel-bottom}}

===Etymology===
From Arabic {{term|lang=ar|مُحَمَّد||tr=muħámmad|[[praise]]d, [[commendable]], [[laudable]]}}, the past participle of {{term|lang=ar|حَمِدَ||tr=ħámida|to [[praise]], [[commend]], [[laud]], [[extol]]}}. From the same triconsonantal root {{ar-root-entry|ح|م|د|nocat=1}} as, but distinct from, {{term|Mahmud|lang=en}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The [[figure]] who [[introduce]]d [[Islam]], the man to whom the [[Quran]] was [[reveal]]ed; considered a prophet by Muslims and [[Baha'i]]s.
#: ''Shias believe that Ali succeeded the prophet '''Mohammad'''.''
# {{given name|male|from=Arabic}} very popular among [[Muslim]]s.

